Variable.chunksizes uses self.data.chunks which triggers loading. We can modify to use self._data if it has chunks attribute? For ZarrArrayWrapper, _data is wrapper; wrapper doesn't have .chunks. But we could check hasattr(self._data,"get_array") and then get array via self._data.get_array() which returns zarr array with .chunks property. So modify chunksizes to:

if hasattr(self._data, "chunks"): use that
elif hasattr(self._data, "get_array"): return Frozen({dim: c for dim,c in zip(self.dims,self._data.get_array().chunks)})
else: return {}

